kind: noninf
question: on a paged plan with an arena, is the default users get after the `Paged` clause goes (unset residency resolves mid-p0-s1, and with it xstream split) not slower in plain decode than today's default (residency off, xstream off)?
term: decode tok/s @ n=96, prose 512 (the corpus's first 512 ids), ctx 3072, A6000, plan a at BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM 27G with BLOOMERY_NVTIER_BYTES=20G, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY and BLOOMERY_XSTREAM unset, BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off, one slot; the changed tree's generate_qwen3moe against main's, (ours - base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -2..10
rounds: 10
margin: 5.0 % lo - h_p at 10 rounds (h_p 2.63 %) must clear it; the derived worst loss is the landing give_back 0.4..0.6 ms of a 32 ms token, 1.2..1.9 %, and the two anchors (ours about 32.3 ms, off floor 31.7 ms plus its fills) put the sign at -2 % at worst
sd: 2.6 % rig-log 09-30#q38seed-ab, as excl-decode.card; the warm regime is likely tighter, not measured
condition: one lease; both builds with Cargo.lock current; every arm a fresh process (BLOOMERY_AB_LOAD=arm), order rotated, one warm-up round discarded; no [cpu-busy], [other-busy], [cold] row, no Xid. Both arms' plan and nvtier budget= and paged= fields equal; the base arm prints `residency unset` off why paged and `xstream=off (unset: no residency or not --place a)`, the ours arm mid-p0-s1 why plan a and `xstream=split ... (unset: --place a with a residency)`; both print `load draft=off`; both print the same greedy tokens. Read beside the ratio, not judged: each arm's pp tok/s at P 512 (the seed moves the prompt), each arm's nvtier fills a token (the arena's warmth after the prompt may differ by arm), ours' landed flips (derived 5.75 a token), late, wait_us and victim wait per job (derived 1.8..2.1 ms with the chain's fills near 0; 2.41 measured with them)
decide-in: land the Paged clause's removal and write the row (tok/s both arms, ratio and interval, pp, flips, late, victim wait, fills) to rig-log with its window named, the arena's warm window after a P 512 prompt
decide-below: read late and wait_us first: the lane's window shrank with the token (2 passes of 32 ms = 64 ms against F x 2.8 ms for F 11.5..23), so late over 2 % of flips puts the term in lane wall and the victims of a window go into one reader job (QD up to 16, derived 12.6 ms for 23 against 55) before any other lever; late 0 with a loss re-derives the landing give_back and the stream's prompt-side cost (pp rows)
decide-above: the seed and the flips explain +2..+10 %; past it read each arm's fills a token: a base arm that kept more fills than ours means the arena's warmth after the prompt differs by arm (the stream's reads), and that is the finding, not the flips
